<title>USA: Bufete's Chile unit wins $18 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Bufete's Chile unit wins $18 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bufete Industrial SA of Mexico said on Thursday that its Chile subsidiary received a US$18.7 million contract for a power project from Foster Wheeler Corp and  Mecanica de la Pena.</p>
<p>The work will involve electromechanical installation as well as minor civil works in Patache's thermoelectric coal-fired plant with 150 megawatts of capacity, Bufete said.</p>
<p>The plant, which is 65 km south of Lquique, Chile, is expected to be completed and begin operations by March 1998, Bufete said.</p>
</text>
